Blockchain Flow Map - notice on the data in this repository

Code: MIT (see LICENSE).

Evidence registry (scripts/registry/addresses.txt and the generated
lib/atlas/known-addresses.ts). Each row quotes, for verification, the public
name tag shown on the address's own page at the named block explorer
(Etherscan, Basescan, Arbiscan, Snowscan, Polygonscan, Optimistic Etherscan or
Tronscan) on the date in the row. The tags are those explorers' data and their
terms of use govern any reuse; this repository grants no licence to
redistribute them. Rows are kept only as the cited evidence behind what the
map draws, and the build refuses a row whose read is older than 180 days.

Entity records (ENTITIES in lib/atlas/known-entities.ts), the dormancy
measurement (scripts/registry/dormancy.json), the code probe
(scripts/registry/code-probe.json), the decision records (docs/) and the
measurement reports (docs/measurements/) are the author's own research and
measurements, citing public regulator, court and company documents where a
jurisdiction is asserted.

Machine-harvested scan output (bulk lists of explorer tags from search or
list endpoints) is not published. The reports that relied on it keep their
figures and name the file as "kept offline".

Geography: Natural Earth (public domain), as world-110m from the world-atlas
project. Stablecoin contract addresses are taken from the issuers' own
published lists (Circle, Tether), cited in the methodology.

The map draws only transfers between wallets whose evidence meets the rules
in docs/METHODOLOGY.md. Nothing here asserts where a person is, who owns an
address, or that any activity is lawful or unlawful.
